            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "1. Definition und Eigenschaften des Logarithmus: - Der Logarithmus "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "\\log_a(b)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " ist diejenige Hochzahl "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "x"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", mit der man die Basis "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " potenzieren muss, um das Argument "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " (den Numerus) zu erhalten:   "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "\\mathbf{\\log_a(b) = x \\quad \\iff \\quad a^x = b} \\quad (a \\in \\mathbb{R}^+ \\setminus \\{1\\}, b \\in \\mathbb{R}^+)",
              "block": true
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " - Spezielle Bezeichnungen:   * "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "\\mathbf{\\lg(x) = \\log_{10}(x)}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ": Zehnerlogarithmus (Briggsscher Logarithmus).   * "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "\\mathbf{\\ln(x) = \\log_e(x)}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ": Natürlicher Logarithmus (Logarithmus naturalis zur Basis "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "e \\approx 2{,}71828"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "). 2. Die drei Logarithmengesetze (für "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "u, v > 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "): - 1. Multiplikationsgesetz (Produktregel):   "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "\\mathbf{\\log_a(u \\cdot v) = \\log_a(u) + \\log_a(v)}",
              "block": true
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " - 2. Divisionsgesetz (Quotientenregel):   "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "\\mathbf{\\log_a\\left(\\frac{u}{v}\\right) = \\log_a(u) - \\log_a(v)}",
              "block": true
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " - 3. Potenzgesetz (Exponentenregel):   "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "\\mathbf{\\log_a(u^r) = r \\cdot \\log_a(u)}",
              "block": true
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " - Basisumrechnung:   "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "\\mathbf{\\log_a(b) = \\frac{\\ln(b)}{\\ln(a)} = \\frac{\\lg(b)}{\\lg(a)}}",
              "block": true
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " 3. Durchrechnung des Beispiels ("
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "3 \\cdot 2^{2x - 1} = 48"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "): - Schritt 1: Isolieren des Exponentialausdrucks:   "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "\\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{2x - 1}}{3} = \\frac{48}{3} \\implies 2^{2x - 1} = 16",
              "block": true
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " - Schritt 2: Logarithmieren (oder Basenvergleich da "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "16 = 2^4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "):   "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "tex": "2^{2x - 1} = 2^4 \\implies 2x - 1 = 4",
              "block": true
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "   (Alternativ über "
